# WFORMTX.KEY - the form dialog's pages, buttons, captions and reserved
# access letters; TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WFORMTX.SNP, which TEST/frmchk.py
# checks.  Item 1 of the seed in every mode, the form of every type, and
# the form of reserved letters (TEST/WFORMT.C), before and after DEL sets
# the help; CTRL+E on a page not the first, and letters typed alone; view
# mode's statics: Tab past them, a '&' in a value, the form of fixed
# formats in view and edit mode, and a loan's row of three dates.
S START
# CTRL-DEL: the form of reserved letters, its 4 free, as the Edit button
# has no letter, its R and N the strip's; no Help button yet.
K CTRL-DEL
S RES
K ESC
# F4: item 1 in view mode, the Overview page, Close and Edit; E and
# SHIFT-E without CTRL switch nothing.
K F4
S VIEW
K E SHIFT-E
S VIEWE
# CTRL-PGDN: Technical, then Notes, then wrapping to Overview.
K CPGDN
S VCTAB
K CPGDN CPGDN
S VCTAB3
K CPGDN
S VWRAP
# CTRL-PGUP: wrapping to Notes, then Acquisition.
K CPGUP
S VCSTAB
K CPGUP
S VCSTAB2
# ALT and a tab's letter: Technical.
K ALT-T
S VALTT
# A click on the second record button ends the dialog with WF_ACT + 1.
M 149 DOWN MID
M 149 UP MID
S VACT
# SHIFT-DEL: a click on tab 1 of the next dialog's strip as it opens.
K SHIFT-DEL
K F4
S VCLICK
K ESC
# F3: item 1 in edit mode, the focus on Category.
K F3
S EDIT
# ALT-A: Acquisition, the focus leaving the hidden Category for Date
# acquired; a negative price typed; ALT-O back to Overview, the focus on
# Category again.
K ALT-A
S EALTA
K ALT-P
T -5
K ALT-O
S EALTO
# OK: the price's check fails, and its page is shown with it.
K ENTER
S ECHECK
# The first record button on a changed record: save first.
M 148 DOWN MID
M 148 UP MID
S ESAVE
K ESC
K Y
S EDONE
# F2: a new item; the first record button says save first.
K F2
S NEW
M 148 DOWN MID
M 148 UP MID
S NEWACT
K ESC
S NEWDONE
# DEL: the help set.  Item 1 in view mode has its Help button, which
# ALT-H presses, the dialog staying; in edit mode too.
K DEL
K F4
S VHELP
K ALT-H
S HELPED
K ESC
K F3
S EHELP
K ESC
# The form of reserved letters with the Help button: its H too.
K CTRL-DEL
S RESHELP
K ESC
# F5: the form of every type, which has no topic, so no Help button: its
# memo alone on the Notes page of its strip.
K F5
S ALL
K CTRL-TAB
S ALLNOTES
K ESC
S DONE
# CTRL+E keeps the page shown: item 1 in view mode on Technical, then in
# edit mode on Technical, the focus on Serial, its first field.
K F4 CTRL-TAB CTRL-E
S EKEEP
K ESC
# The password form in view mode on its Notes page: CTRL+E edits it
# there, the focus on the memo.
K SHIFT-F1 CTRL-TAB CTRL-E
S MKEEP
K ESC
# A tab's letter alone on a control that takes no characters: T on the
# Close button, five Shift+Tabs back from the strip, past the identity
# row's model and maker, Help and Edit, shows Technical, the focus
# staying on Close.
K F4 STAB STAB STAB STAB STAB
T t
S PLAINT
K ESC
# A field's letter alone on the strip, for a field of a page not shown:
# P shows Acquisition and moves the focus to Price paid, the dialog
# staying.
K F3 STAB
T p
S PLAINP
K ESC
S LAST
# View mode opens on the strip; Tab passes the statics, which have no
# Tab stop, to the read-only fields of free text longer than their box
# (Part of, Tags), then the first record button, then on to Close; on
# Notes, the memo is the strip's next.
K F4 TAB TAB TAB
S VTAB
K TAB TAB TAB TAB
S VTABC
K ESC
K F4 CTRL-SHIFT-TAB TAB
S VTABN
K ESC
# No label shows a letter in view mode: Alt and Category's edit-mode
# letter, then Price paid's typed alone on the strip, move nothing.
K F4 ALT-C
T p
S VALTC
K ESC
# A '&' in a value: typed into the form of every type, kept by OK, then
# shown as it is in view mode, no access letter (its R would be the
# strip's).
K F5
T R&R Repairs
K ALT-C DOWN ENTER
K F6
S VAMP
K ESC
# SHIFT-F6: the form of fixed formats, one page, the focus on Close,
# each value at its widest held whole by its static.
K SHIFT-F6
S VFIX
K ESC
# SHIFT-F5: the same form in edit mode, each control as wide as its
# static was in view mode.
K SHIFT-F5
S EFIX
K ESC
# CTRL-F6: a returned loan, whose out, due and return dates share a row
# of INV's table; the return date, which the row has no room for at its
# width, goes on to a line of its own, held whole.
K CTRL-F6
S LOAN
K ESC
S END
